ke the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"config.yaml\", \"contents\": \"    Indented line 1\\n    Indented line 2\\n    New indented line\\n    Blank line above\\n    Indented line 3\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_79bf5a2671c1"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nGuidelines:\n- Do not infer missing logic\n- Do not create domain-specific content\n- Only manipulate the text the user describes\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files\n- If the user asks to confirm or check contents without changes, only read the file"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Check the contents of `document.md` and confirm what's in it. Don't make any changes."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file to check its contents.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"document.md\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line", "tool_call_id": "call_3217b01f7d4c"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The file `document.md` contains:\n\nLine 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line\n\nNo changes were made as requested."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it's already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that's actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `file.txt`.\n\nInsert a new line after line 2: 'Line 2.5: Inserted line'"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"file.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "Line 1: First line\nLine 2: Second line\nLine 3: Third line", "tool_call_id": "call_c75a743c1cee"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"file.txt\", \"contents\": \"Line 1: First line\\nLine 2: Second line\\nLine 2.5: Inserted line\\nLine 3: Third line\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_4e8f98ae4853"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create new content that wasn't in the original file\n- Do NOT \"fix\" or \"improve\" the file content\n- Do NOT add domain-specific logic or code\n- ONLY perform the exact text manipulation the user requests\n- If the user says \"replace X with Y\", ONLY replace X with Y - nothing else\n- If the user says \"add the content 'X'\", add ONLY 'X' - nothing else\n- If the file is EMPTY and user says \"add content 'X'\", the file should contain ONLY 'X' (no other content)\n- Do NOT add example content like \"line1: first line\" or \"existing content\" unless it's already in the file\n- Content to add/remove is usually specified in single or double quotes: 'text' or \"text\"\n- Extract the exact content from quotes - do not modify or interpret it\n- When reading a file, use ONLY the content that's actually in the file (from read_file tool response)\n- Do NOT infer or add content that wasn't in the file you read\n- Preserve all other content exactly as it was (if any exists)\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely and literally\n- Use tools to read, modify, and write files"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit the file at `input.txt`.\n\nReplace the word \"sample\" with \"example\""}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll read the file, make the requested changes, and save it.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: read_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"input.txt\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "sample text\nmore sample text", "tool_call_id": "call_da1f34fa6f1d"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I'll make the requested changes and save the file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"input.txt\", \"contents\": \"example text\\nmore example text\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_51c5c591139d"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "Your job is to create and edit files using tools exactly as the user instructs.\n\nYou have access to these tools:\n- `read_file(path)`: Read the contents of a file at the given path\n- `write_file(path, contents)`: Write contents to a file at the given path\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n- Do NOT infer or generate content based on file extensions\n- Do NOT create default/example content unless the user explicitly requests it\n- If the user says \"create a file X\" without specifying content, create an EMPTY file\n- Do NOT add \"test: 1\" or any default content to YAML files\n- Do NOT add default structure to JSON files\n- Only create the exact content the user describes\n- If no content is specified, use write_file with empty contents: \"\"\n- Follow the user's instructions precisely"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Create a new file at `data.json`"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll create the new file.\n\n<tool_call>\nname: write_file\narguments: {\"path\": \"data.json\", \"contents\": \"\"}\n</tool_call>"}, {"role": "tool", "content": "File written successfully.", "tool_call_id": "call_556ef5d766ee"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Done. The file has been created."}]}
